    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.6,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.06,
    "rationale": "I diluted the 18 h aliquot and scaled each reading back up by its dilution factor. The undiluted reading was 1.553. The 2-fold dilution read 0.8026, which scales to 1.605. The 10-fold dilution read 0.1681 and 0.1627, which scales to about 1.65. The 20-fold dilution read 0.0782, which scales to 1.564. All four estimates agree within about 6%. If the reader were saturating at about 1.6, the diluted samples would scale up to clearly higher values, and they do not. The plateau from about 7 h onward therefore reflects real stationary phase, not detector saturation. The small excess in the 10-fold dilution is within replicate and pipetting noise and shows no trend with dilution."
